# Addressable — `rbs collection` correction overlay (issue #2857).
#
# gem_rbs_collection's `gems/addressable/*/addressable.rbs` declares
# `Addressable::URI.parse` as `(String | URI uri) -> instance`, but
# `Addressable::URI.parse(nil)` returns nil, so `Addressable::URI.parse(x)`
# on a `String?` — the mastodon `fetch_link_card_service.rb` shape — drew a
# false `call.argument-type-mismatch` on correct code.
#
# Unlike the activesupport overlay this directory does NOT ride the ADR-72
# `:missing` gate: it loads only when `rbs collection` supplies the gem's
# RBS (`:rbs_collection` coverage — `Environment::GEM_OVERLAY_COVERAGE_SOURCES`).
# The deferred-signature plan (#2422) then composes this declaration over the
# collection's copy as an overload continuation, so `parse(nil)` binds nil
# while `parse(String | URI)` keeps the URI answer and a `String?` argument
# mismatches nothing. Under `:missing` coverage — no sigs at all — the
# overlay stays unloaded on purpose: this partial `Addressable::URI`
# declaration would make every member it omits (`host`, `path`, …) a false
# `call.undefined-method`, which is worse than the `Dynamic` silence a
# sig-less gem already has.
module Addressable
  class URI
    # Two arms, URI-carrying first — the order is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
    # `Addressable::URI` is RBS-known but not loadable in the analyzer's host
    # process, so `NilClass`-vs-`Addressable::URI` acceptance answers `maybe`,
    # and the overload selector's strict pass takes the FIRST maybe-match: a
    # leading `(::NilClass)` arm would shadow this one and type
    # `parse(existing_uri)` as `nil`. With the URI arm first it answers `yes`
    # and wins; `nil` still reaches the second arm.
    #
    # `::NilClass`, not the `nil` keyword: they accept the same arguments, but
    # RBS types `nil` as `Types::Bases::Nil`, which the
    # `call.argument-type-mismatch` non-nil channel reads as "undecidable →
    # admits", silently dropping `Addressable::URI.parse(123)`. `NilClass` is
    # a `ClassInstance`, so the channel still refutes what no overload admits.
    #
    # The collection's own `(String | URI uri) -> instance` stays reachable as
    # the `| ...` fallback the deferred plan appends.
    def self.parse: (String | URI uri) -> URI | (::NilClass) -> nil
  end
end
